error[E0115]: `par` takes a tuple of two or more expressions
 --> fork_join_errors.ck:4:9
  |
4 |     par (f x)
  |         ^^^^^
  = help: write `par (f x, g y)`; the components are evaluated in parallel

error[E0116]: `fork` must be bound to a future
 --> fork_join_errors.ck:7:5
  |
7 |     fork using sched
  |     ^^^^
  = help: write `f <- fork … using sched` on its own line; use `_ <-` to ignore the future

error[E0112]: `join` needs a scheduler capability: `using sched`
  --> fork_join_errors.ck:11:20
   |
11 |     r <- join x = p
   |                    ^ expected `using`
   = help: scheduling is an effect; pass the `Sched` capability, e.g. `f <- join … using sched`

